IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch4-fourth-schedule.l4: the Fourth Schedule (decisions of the General Division that are not appealable).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 5830-5954).  Answers seam 4 of PLAN.md; the asking section is s 29(b), in scja1's range.
-- "The Schedule bars an appeal" is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Schedule itself takes the case out (para 1 "except if", para 2, para 3(1) "unless",
-- para 4(1) "except") or where the limb's own "where" is not met; NOTHING where the decision is outside the Schedule's scope.

§ `Fourth Schedule: decisions of the General Division that are not appealable`

-- The facts about a decision that the Fourth Schedule turns on and that the core's Decision does not hold.
DECLARE `sch 4 facts about the decision` HAS
    `a Judge made the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the decision involves the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the party seeking to appeal proves a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appeal is against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action was ordered, with the consent of all the parties, to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the order refused a request, made with the consent of all the parties, for the expedited procedure` IS A BOOLEAN

-- When the agreement that a decision is final was made (para 3(2)(a)).
DECLARE `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) when the agreement was made` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) before the decision was made`
    `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) after the decision was made`
    `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) at the same time as the decision`

-- Helper for the limbs below: one answer from several limbs.  Any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE; limbs that all fail give JUST FALSE
-- (s 29(b) hands "a case specified in the Fourth Schedule" to this list); a limb that cannot be answered leaves the whole NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the limbs taken together` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING limbs
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any of the following cases" [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- An order that gives (in whole or on condition) or refuses; "made, being neither a grant nor a refusal" is neither.
GIVEN way IS A `Way an order went`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the order gave` MEANS
    way EQUALS `granted unconditionally` OR way EQUALS `granted on condition that the party pays into court or gives security for the sum claimed`

GIVEN way IS A `Way an order went`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the order gave or refused` MEANS
    `sch 4 the order gave` way OR way EQUALS refused

-- The Schedule's scope: "Decisions of General Division".  The Singapore International Commercial Court is read as within it through s 18C (fork S3-K1).
-- The Family Division of the High Court is spoken of both as part of the General Division and apart from it (paras 2, Fifth Schedule paras 2(2)(b), 4, 5(1)): not covered.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER decision's `made by`
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the Fourth Schedule says "General Division" and nothing here says whether the Family Division of the High Court is part of it
    WHEN `Family Division of the High Court` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule speaks of decisions of the General Division only as its subject
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5877 | 2. Paragraph 1 does not apply to any decision, judgment or order of the Family
-- src:5878 | Division of the High Court involving the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction
-- src:5879 | mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014.
@ref Fourth Schedule para 2 (src:5877-5879)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` MEANS
    IF decision's `made by` EQUALS `Family Division of the High Court`
       AND decision's `in the exercise of` EQUALS `appellate jurisdiction`
       AND decision's `nature of the proceeding` EQUALS `a civil proceeding`
       AND facts's `the decision involves the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 2 speaks only of a decision of the Family Division "involving the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:5841 | (b) where the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1(b) (src:5841)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` MEANS
    IF decision's `made by consent of the parties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5847 | (h) where a Judge makes an order giving or refusing further and better
-- src:5849 | particulars;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1(h) (src:5847-5849)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` MEANS
    IF facts's `a Judge made the order`
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `further and better particulars`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave or refused` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Judge makes an order giving or refusing further and better particulars"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5858 | (i) where a Judge makes an order giving permission to amend a pleading,
-- src:5859 | except if —
-- src:5861 | (i) the application for such permission is made after the expiry of
-- src:5862 | any relevant period of limitation current at the date of issue of
-- src:5863 | the originating claim; and
-- src:5867 | (ii) the amendment is an amendment to correct the name of a party
-- src:5868 | or to alter the capacity in which a party sues, or the effect of the
-- src:5869 | amendment will be to add or substitute a new cause of action;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1(i) (src:5858-5869)
-- "except if (i) ... and (ii) ...": the permission to amend is out of this limb when it was applied for after a relevant limitation period
-- had expired AND the amendment corrects a party's name or capacity, or adds or substitutes a new cause of action.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` MEANS
    IF facts's `a Judge made the order`
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `amending a pleading`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN IF facts's `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired`
            AND (facts's `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues`
                 OR facts's `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except if (i) the application for such permission is made after the expiry of any relevant period of limitation ... and (ii) the amendment is an amendment to correct the name of a party or to alter the capacity in which a party sues, or the effect of the amendment will be to add or substitute a new cause of action"
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Judge makes an order giving permission to amend a pleading"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5873 | (j) where a Judge makes an order refusing security for costs;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1(j) (src:5873)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1(j) a Judge refuses security for costs` MEANS
    IF facts's `a Judge made the order`
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `security for costs`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS refused
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Judge makes an order refusing security for costs"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5875 | (k) where a Judge makes an order giving or refusing interrogatories.
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1(k) (src:5875)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1(k) a Judge gives or refuses interrogatories` MEANS
    IF facts's `a Judge made the order`
       AND decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS interrogatories
       AND `sch 4 the order gave or refused` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Judge makes an order giving or refusing interrogatories"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5837 | 1. Subject to paragraph 2, an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the
-- src:5838 | General Division in any of the following cases:
@ref Fourth Schedule para 1 (opening words) (src:5837-5838)
-- Paragraph 1: "Subject to paragraph 2, an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the General Division in any of the following cases".
-- Paragraph 2 takes a Family Division appellate decision out first (JUST FALSE); then the limbs (b), (h), (i), (j), (k) (limbs (a), (c) to (g) are shown deleted).
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` decision facts
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph 2" and "Paragraph 1 does not apply to any decision, judgment or order of the Family Division of the High Court involving the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` decision
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            `sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST
                  `sch 4 para 1(b) the judgment or order is made by consent of the parties` decision
                , `sch 4 para 1(h) a Judge gives or refuses further and better particulars` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 1(i) a Judge gives permission to amend a pleading, unless the exception applies` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 1(j) a Judge refuses security for costs` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 1(k) a Judge gives or refuses interrogatories` decision facts)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 speaks of "a decision of the General Division"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5890 | (2) An agreement mentioned in sub‑paragraph (1) —
-- src:5892 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the agreement
-- src:5893 | relates is made; and
-- src:5895 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:5896 | sub‑paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that
-- src:5897 | part of the decision.
@ref Fourth Schedule para 3(2) (src:5890-5897)
GIVEN timing IS A `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) when the agreement was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 3(2)(a) the agreement counts whenever it was made` MEANS
    CONSIDER timing
    WHEN `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) before the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) after the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says the agreement "may be made before or after the decision" and says nothing of an agreement made at the same moment
    WHEN `sch 4 para 3(2)(a) at the same time as the decision` THEN NOTHING

-- src:5890 | (2) An agreement mentioned in sub‑paragraph (1) —
-- src:5892 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the agreement
-- src:5893 | relates is made; and
-- src:5895 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:5896 | sub‑paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that
-- src:5897 | part of the decision.
@ref Fourth Schedule para 3(2)(b) (src:5890-5897)
-- When the agreement relates to part of a decision, the bar reaches that part only.  Appealing another part is outside the bar.
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT facts's `the agreement that the decision is final relates only to part of the decision`
       OR facts's `the appeal is against the part of the decision that the agreement relates to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references in sub-paragraph (1) to a decision are to be read as references to that part of the decision"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5881 | 3.—(1) An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the General Division,
-- src:5882 | where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that
-- src:5883 | the decision is final, unless the party seeking to appeal proves that —
-- src:5885 | (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or
-- src:5887 | (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the
-- src:5888 | proceedings resulting in the decision.
@ref Fourth Schedule para 3(1) (src:5881-5888)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` decision
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF decision's `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final`
        THEN IF facts's `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality`
                OR facts's `the party seeking to appeal proves a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice`
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party seeking to appeal proves that (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice"
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE `sch 4 para 3(2)(b) the part of the decision appealed against is covered by the agreement` facts
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 3(1) speaks of "a decision of the General Division"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5909 | (a) an order that the Court has no jurisdiction, or should not exercise
-- src:5910 | jurisdiction, to hear the action;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(a) (src:5909-5910)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(a) the order is that the Court has no jurisdiction or should not exercise it` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `whether the court has jurisdiction or should exercise it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order that the Court has no jurisdiction, or should not exercise jurisdiction, to hear the action"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5919 | (b) an order for summary judgment;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(b) (src:5919)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(b) the order is for summary judgment` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `summary judgment`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for summary judgment"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5921 | (c) an order refusing to set aside a default judgment, regardless of how the
-- src:5922 | default judgment was obtained (including whether by reason of a
-- src:5923 | breach of an order of court or otherwise);
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(c) (src:5921-5923)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(c) the order refuses to set aside a default judgment` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `setting aside a default judgment`
       AND decision's `the order`'s `way it went` EQUALS refused
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order refusing to set aside a default judgment, regardless of how the default judgment was obtained"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5925 | (d) an order for the striking out of the action;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(d) (src:5925)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(d) the order is for the striking out of the action` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `striking out an action or a matter commenced by originating process`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for the striking out of the action"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5927 | (e) an order for the action (or part of the action) to be dismissed, or for
-- src:5928 | judgment to be entered, upon the striking out or amendment of any
-- src:5929 | pleading or part of any pleading;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(e) (src:5927-5929)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(e) the order dismisses the action or enters judgment upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `dismissing an action, or entering judgment, upon striking out or amendment of a pleading`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for the action (or part of the action) to be dismissed, or for judgment to be entered, upon the striking out or amendment of any pleading or part of any pleading"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5931 | (f) an order giving or refusing permission to amend a pleading, where —
-- src:5933 | (i) the application for permission is made after the expiry of any
-- src:5934 | relevant period of limitation current at the date of issue of the
-- src:5935 | originating claim; and
-- src:5937 | (ii) the amendment is an amendment to correct the name of a party
-- src:5938 | or to alter the capacity in which a party sues, or the effect of the
-- src:5939 | amendment will be to add or substitute a new cause of action;
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(f) (src:5931-5939)
-- Unlike para 1(i), this limb names the same two conditions as the case that IS excepted from the bar: "where (i) ... and (ii) ...".
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `amending a pleading`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave or refused` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
       AND facts's `permission to amend was applied for after a relevant period of limitation had expired`
       AND (facts's `the amendment corrects the name of a party or alters the capacity in which a party sues`
            OR facts's `the amendment adds or substitutes a new cause of action`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order giving or refusing permission to amend a pleading, where (i) the application for permission is made after the expiry of any relevant period of limitation ... and (ii) the amendment is an amendment to correct the name of a party ... or the effect of the amendment will be to add or substitute a new cause of action"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5941 | (g) an order giving security for costs (subject to obtaining permission to
-- src:5942 | appeal as required in paragraph 3(i) of the Fifth Schedule);
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(g) (src:5941-5942)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(g) the order gives security for costs` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `security for costs`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order giving security for costs"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5944 | (h) an order for a stay of proceedings; or
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(h) (src:5944)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(h) the order is for a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    IF decision's `the order`'s about EQUALS `a stay of proceedings`
       AND `sch 4 the order gave` (decision's `the order`'s `way it went`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for a stay of proceedings"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5946 | (i) a judgment given after the trial of an action (whether or not all parties
-- src:5947 | participated in the trial).
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1)(i) (src:5946-5947)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1)(i) the decision is a judgment given after the trial of an action` MEANS
    IF decision's `made after the trial of an action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judgment given after the trial of an action (whether or not all parties participated in the trial)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5903 | 4.—(1) Where an action is, with the consent of all the parties, ordered by the
-- src:5904 | General Division to be dealt with in accordance with an expedited procedure
-- src:5905 | under the Rules of Court that includes restrictions in this sub‑paragraph on the
-- src:5906 | bringing of an appeal, an appeal cannot be brought against any decision of a Judge
-- src:5907 | in the action except —
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1) (src:5903-5907)
-- The decisions that para 4(1)(a) to (i) leave appealable, taken together.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1) the decision is one of those that remain appealable` MEANS
    `sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST
          `sch 4 para 4(1)(a) the order is that the Court has no jurisdiction or should not exercise it` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(b) the order is for summary judgment` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(c) the order refuses to set aside a default judgment` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(d) the order is for the striking out of the action` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(e) the order dismisses the action or enters judgment upon striking out or amendment of a pleading` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(f) the order gives or refuses permission to amend a pleading after limitation expired` decision facts
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(g) the order gives security for costs` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(h) the order is for a stay of proceedings` decision
        , `sch 4 para 4(1)(i) the decision is a judgment given after the trial of an action` decision)

-- src:5903 | 4.—(1) Where an action is, with the consent of all the parties, ordered by the
-- src:5904 | General Division to be dealt with in accordance with an expedited procedure
-- src:5905 | under the Rules of Court that includes restrictions in this sub‑paragraph on the
-- src:5906 | bringing of an appeal, an appeal cannot be brought against any decision of a Judge
-- src:5907 | in the action except —
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(1) (src:5903-5907)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` decision
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF facts's `the action was ordered, with the consent of all the parties, to be dealt with under an expedited procedure that restricts appeals`
           AND facts's `a Judge made the order`
        THEN CONSIDER `sch 4 para 4(1) the decision is one of those that remain appealable` decision facts
             -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an appeal cannot be brought against any decision of a Judge in the action except (a) ... (i)"
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb of the exception could not be answered
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an action is, with the consent of all the parties, ordered by the General Division to be dealt with in accordance with an expedited procedure under the Rules of Court that includes restrictions in this sub-paragraph on the bringing of an appeal"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 4(1) speaks of an action ordered "by the General Division"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5949 | (2) An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the General Division
-- src:5950 | where a Judge makes an order refusing a request made with the consent of all the
-- src:5951 | parties for an action to be dealt with in accordance with the expedited procedure
-- src:5952 | under the Rules of Court mentioned in sub‑paragraph (1).
@ref Fourth Schedule para 4(2) (src:5949-5952)
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4(2) an appeal cannot be brought against an order refusing the expedited procedure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` decision
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF facts's `a Judge made the order`
           AND facts's `the order refused a request, made with the consent of all the parties, for the expedited procedure`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a Judge makes an order refusing a request made with the consent of all the parties for an action to be dealt with in accordance with the expedited procedure"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 4(2) speaks of "a decision of the General Division"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5837 | 1. Subject to paragraph 2, an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of the
-- src:5838 | General Division in any of the following cases:
@ref Fourth Schedule (seam 4) (src:5837-5838)
-- Seam 4 of PLAN.md.  JUST TRUE: a paragraph of the Schedule bars the appeal.  JUST FALSE: the Schedule itself takes the case out, or no paragraph lists it.
-- NOTHING: the decision is outside the Schedule's scope.  A caller never turns a NOTHING into a FALSE.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      facts IS A `sch 4 facts about the decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the Fourth Schedule says no appeal can be brought` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 para 2 paragraph 1 does not apply to the decision` decision facts
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 does not apply to any decision, judgment or order of the Family Division of the High Court involving the exercise of the appellate civil jurisdiction mentioned in section 23 of the Family Justice Act 2014"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `sch 4 the decision is one of the General Division` decision
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            `sch 4 the limbs taken together` (LIST
                  `sch 4 para 1 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 3(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision the parties agreed in writing is final` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 4(1) an appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Judge in an action under the expedited procedure` decision facts
                , `sch 4 para 4(2) an appeal cannot be brought against an order refusing the expedited procedure` decision facts)
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Schedule is headed "Decisions of General Division that are not appealable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
